# Creatio requests for the REST Client extension (VS Code) or the Rider / Visual Studio HTTP client.
#
# 1. Fill in @baseUrl, @login, @password (never commit real credentials).
# 2. Run "Login". The response sets cookies (.ASPXAUTH, BPMCSRF, ...); both clients keep them
#    for the following requests automatically.
# 3. Copy the value of the BPMCSRF cookie from the Login response (Set-Cookie header) into @csrf.
#    Creatio rejects state-changing calls without a BPMCSRF header equal to that cookie.
# 4. Put ids of test applications into the @app* variables (open the record, copy the id from the URL).
@baseUrl = https://your-instance.creatio.com
@login = Supervisor
@password = change-me
@csrf = paste-BPMCSRF-cookie-value-here

# Applications prepared for each case (see README, section Creatio):
@appNew = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@appApproved = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Login (cookie-based authentication)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ServiceModel/AuthService.svc/Login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "UserName": "{{login}}",
  "UserPassword": "{{password}}"
}

### Score — success (application in status NEW with valid fields)
# Expected: {"ScoreResult":{"success":true,"errorCode":null,"statusCode":"APPROVED"|"REVIEW"|"REJECTED",...}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/0/rest/UsrLoanScoringService/Score
Content-Type: application/json
BPMCSRF: {{csrf}}

{ "applicationId": "{{appNew}}" }

### Score — APP_NOT_FOUND (random id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/0/rest/UsrLoanScoringService/Score
Content-Type: application/json
BPMCSRF: {{csrf}}

{ "applicationId": "6f1c2b9e-dead-beef-0000-000000000000" }

### Score — INVALID_STATUS (an application already scored, e.g. APPROVED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/0/rest/UsrLoanScoringService/Score
Content-Type: application/json
BPMCSRF: {{csrf}}

{ "applicationId": "{{appApproved}}" }

### Score — VALIDATION_ERROR
# The listener rejects out-of-range values on every ORM save, so such an application can only
# exist if it was written around the ORM (direct SQL) or before the package was installed.
# With no such record this request returns another code; see README, section Creatio.
POST {{baseUrl}}/0/rest/UsrLoanScoringService/Score
Content-Type: application/json
BPMCSRF: {{csrf}}

{ "applicationId": "{{appNew}}" }

### Score — SCORING_UNAVAILABLE
# Preparation: UsrScoringUseMock = false, UsrScoringApiUrl = http://127.0.0.1:9 (nothing listens).
# Expected: errorCode SCORING_UNAVAILABLE, statusCode NEW (rolled back).
POST {{baseUrl}}/0/rest/UsrLoanScoringService/Score
Content-Type: application/json
BPMCSRF: {{csrf}}

{ "applicationId": "{{appNew}}" }

### Score — SCORING_ERROR
# Preparation: UsrScoringUseMock = false, UsrScoringApiUrl = the tunnel URL of the Scoring API,
# UsrScoringApiKey = wrong-key. The API answers 401 -> errorCode SCORING_ERROR, statusCode NEW.
POST {{baseUrl}}/0/rest/UsrLoanScoringService/Score
Content-Type: application/json
BPMCSRF: {{csrf}}

{ "applicationId": "{{appNew}}" }

### Score without BPMCSRF header — rejected by Creatio before reaching the service
POST {{baseUrl}}/0/rest/UsrLoanScoringService/Score
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applicationId": "{{appNew}}" }
